                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>In a memorandum to the President, dated May 11, 1954, Secretary Dulles commented on unsettled labor conditions
                    in Honduras, reports of suspicious movements of planes and men from Guatemala to
                    Honduras, and the preparation of a plan for providing direct military assistance
                    to Honduras, in the event that the Honduran Government requested such assistance
                    under the provisions of the Rio Treaty. The memorandum is printed on <ref
                        target="#pg1303">page 1303</ref>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
